ses the Payphone to  call Douglas but the call is not  answered soon a mysterious man appears  and Fuller follows him outside the two  chat for a while but shockingly the man  stabs Fuller with a knife and murders  him the next morning Douglas wakes up  and finds blood-stained clothes in his  laundry buckets he's obviously confused  where it came from but before he can  investigate he gets a call from  detective McBain of the LAPD and learns  about his mentor Fuller's murderer the  two then meet at Fuller's apartment here  it is revealed that Douglas had a close  relationship with Fuller and that they  were working on a highly classified  project which is the virtual reality  world of 1937. the detective mentions  that Douglas has become the prime  suspect of the murder as he was the last  person Fuller tried to contact before  his death just then the two encounter a  distraught young woman named Jane in  Fuller's bedroom when Douglas questions  her she reveals that she is the only  daughter of Mr Fuller and is only  returned from Paris after learning of  her dad's death she got back awfully  fast Douglas then leaves the two alone  for interrogation while he goes to the  VR lab there he talks with his co-worker  Jason Whitney and the latter reveals  that Fuller was secretly testing the  1937 La simulation Douglas is caught off  guard as he was under the impression  that the company was months away from  the first trial  afterwards Douglas returns home and goes  through his audio messages in one of  them an anxious Fuller tells him that he  has found something incredible and that  he has left a letter for him inside the  1937 VR simulation because he fears his  own death is imminent Douglas then heads  straight back to the VR lab and tells  his colleague Jason about the message he  asks him about the VR characters Fuller  interacted with last night and also  Reveals His desire to go into the VR  simulation Jason is naturally against  this however Douglas is adamant on  finding answers as now even the police  are starting to suspect him of being the  murderer moreover he himself is not sure  if he's innocent because all evidence  points to him and he can't even remember  what happened that night Jason finally  agrees to let him go into the system but  only for two hours shortly after the  preparation for the simulation commences  and after a few adjustments Douglas is  sent back to 1937 La Jason assigns him  the role of a wealthy Bank clerk named  Joan Ferguson at first Douglas who now  possesses Ferguson seems confused and  tries to process everything that just  just happened but soon he has taken  aback by the accurate representation of  the city which makes him smile for a  while then he takes a break from  Ferguson's work and goes to meet  Fuller's 1937 double named grierson who  is a historian the two talk for a while  but surprisingly grierson asserts that  he doesn't remember writing any letter  to him here it is revealed that once a  person leaves the simulation his or her  double will immediately forget about the  events that occurred while they were  under control but with that being said  grierson admits that he has a clue  probably because he remembers some  fragments of his memories this leads  Douglas to the bartender Jerry Ashton  surprisingly Ashton turns out to be the  1937 double of Jason which takes Douglas  by surprise however he ignores it and  inquires if Fuller left a message for  him the bartender feigns ignorance and  denies receiving any messages it seems  like he's bitter as he has now learned  the truth about being a simulation  hearing this Douglas is puzzled and he  suddenly begins to hallucinate he  quickly rushes to the bathroom suffering  from a seizure before collapsing on the  ground back in the 1997 VR lab warning  signs go off and Jason terminates the  connection and brings Douglas back Jason  explains that the unit started glitching  because Douglas spent two hours inside  the simulation which is double the  recommended time after collecting  himself Douglas shares his experience  inside the simulation and happily tells  Jason that the VR very much Works  meanwhile in the 1937 simulation Ashton  the bartender speaks with John Ferguson  once he emerges from the washroom  however Ferguson is puzzled how he got  to the hotel and doesn't recall having  any conversation with Ashton back in  1997 a waiter named Tom Jones from the  bar outside which Fuller was killed in  shows up at the company HQ he speaks  with Douglas privately and mentions that  he saw the crime taking place while the  latter asks about the killer Jones  reveals that it was none other than  Douglas himself he then demands a large  Ransom to keep his mouth shut about the  murder Douglas is naturally puzzled as  he doesn't recall killing his own Mentor  however suddenly something takes over  him as if if he has become possessed  Douglas then attacks Jones with  tremendous rage prompting him to run  away at this point he has become  extremely confused and doesn't know whom  to trust and whom not to later Douglas  takes Jane out for dinner and tells her  everything it's clear that the two have  started to like each other and Jane  advises him to walk away from all of  this before he gets hurt like her father  did Douglas thanks her for her concern  and soon the two start dancing one thing  leads to another and the two start  making out following the romantic dinner  Douglas returns home and later that  night several police officers storm into  his place and take him to the station on  suspicion of the murder of Tom Jones  detective McBain reveals that Jones came  to the police station and gave a  statement claiming he saw Fuller leaving  with Douglas on the night he was  murdered however Jones was brutally  murdered last night the damning evidence  is enough to keep Douglas behind bars  but the very next morning Jane arrives  at the station and bails him out she  even vouches for Douglas saying that he  was present with her during the time  Jones was killed Jane is sure that  Douglas is Innocent but he feels that it  just because he doesn't remember  anything doesn't mean he's not the  killer searching for answers Douglas  goes straight to the VR lab and  teleports his Consciousness into John  Ferguson's body in 1937 La he then goes  to meet grierson Fuller's VR double it's  late at night and the old man doesn't  want to talk but Douglas promises to  reveal why he sometimes wakes up in  unknown places if he comes with him  shortly after the two go to the Wilshire  Grand Hotel and grierson reveals that in  the last three days he's been having  strange memory flashes where he finds  himself at the hotel time and time again  hearing this Douglas becomes happy and  he pressures grierson to recall if he  gave someone a letter or a note after  much effort the old man finally  remembers giving a letter to Ashton the  bartender however before Douglas can  make his way to the counter Ashton runs  away Douglas chases him to the basement  and eventually confronts him  unfortunately Ashton pulls out a gun and  demands to know what's going on Douglas  pretends to know nothing but Ashton  tells him that he noticed Douglas  switching places with Ferguson he also  reveals that he read the letter left by  Fuller her Ashton knows that he is an  artificial creation and the world around  them is not real to see for himself  following the instructions on the letter  Ashton drove to a place he would never  go to otherwise to his shock after  reaching a certain point he found out  that there was no life it's simply a  computer simulation sounds like Ashton's  been getting into the bath salts Douglas  is puzzled as to why Fuller would write  to him about the limitations of  simulation because he already knows them  but before he can say anything Ashton  threatens to kill him for messing with  people's minds and tries drowning him in  a pool Douglas fights for his life and  in 